        "rationale": "**Obligations**\n- The struct pairs `content` with `fingerprint`, and `Snapshot::new` builds one.\n- For node reads, the SDK builds the `Snapshot` from the contents `Domain::node_content` returns. The fingerprint is the contents' own `NodeContents::fingerprint`. No additional read happens.\n- The `Clone`/`Debug` impls, `#[non_exhaustive]` and the public field shapes are structural. They have no independent observable behaviour here.\n- `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint` is cited context. I did not reassess it.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Constructor and fields:** `tests/contracts.rs#fn[callers_can_pair_content_with_its_fingerprint]` calls `Snapshot::new(vec![1,2], fp)` from an external test crate. It asserts both public fields. That also shows the type can be built from outside the crate despite `non_exhaustive`.\n- **Fingerprint comes from the contents:** `tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` reads a snapshot through `read_snapshot`. It asserts `snapshot.content.fingerprint() == snapshot.fingerprint` and `fingerprint.value == \"before\"`. After the underlying data changes, the content and fingerprint still describe \"before\". It also asserts the domain's `reads == [1]`, so there is exactly one read.\n- **Exact reads, no extra read:** `src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` checks `read_snapshot(...).fingerprint == fp(\"before\")`. It checks that later reads give distinct \"after\" snapshots. It also checks that the recorded read sequence is `[1,1,1,2]`, one domain read per SDK call, including the failing read of node 2.\n- **Empty and large Unicode contents:** `src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]` covers empty and multi-byte large contents. It asserts the snapshot's content and fingerprint, with `reads == [1,1]` for two reads. A failed read records no dependency.\n- **Agent-driven reads and Habeas domain:**\n  - `src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` and `src/agent/tests.rs#fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]` assert the recorded node fingerprints. They check the number of reads and the fingerprint content.\n  - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` compares the retained contents' fingerprint with `node_content(...).fingerprint()` on the real Habeas domain.\n- **Structural obligations:** `Clone`, `Debug` and `non_exhaustive` are derive-level or compile-time. `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the export inventory. They need no separate behavioural test."
      }
